<section image-layout="blank" id="dgwqTqMjen" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="KjI3GeAm2K" vertical-align="center" colspan="25"><p role="eyebrow">Evidence bearing 02</p><h2>Relic light on every horizon</h2><display size="md" font-size="44pt">≈380,000 years</display><p font-size="18pt">The universe became transparent enough for light to travel freely; expansion has since cooled that relic light into microwaves.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><h4>Cosmic microwave background</h4><p font-size="18pt">We detect it across the sky—not from one central blast port.</p><p font-size="13pt">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="5_L16S4Eom" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><labels><label variant="outline">Conceptual all-sky direction map</label></labels><h3>Relic light arrives from around us</h3><freeform-block w="500" h="292"><shape preset="roundRect" w="500" h="292" fill="surface" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="40" y="42" w="420" h="196" fill="surface" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="72" y="78" w="178" h="70" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="78" w="178" h="70" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="line" x="48" y="145" w="202" h="4" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="145" w="202" h="4" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="line" x="82" y="148" w="168" h="66" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1" flip-h="true"></shape><shape preset="line" x="250" y="148" w="168" h="66" stroke="palette-5" stroke-width="1"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="82" y="72" w="34" h="24" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="144" y="102" w="45" h="28" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="215" y="65" w="30" h="22" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="285" y="92" w="54" h="30" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="365" y="66" w="38" h="26" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="105" y="160" w="52" h="30" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="181" y="184" w="40" h="24" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="296" y="166" w="38" h="26" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="370" y="177" w="48" h="27" fill="palette-3" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="236" y="134" w="28" h="28" fill="palette-4" stroke="accent" stroke-width="2"></shape><box type="content" x="195" y="164" w="110"><p font-size="16pt" align="center"><b>Observer</b></p></box><box type="content" x="55" y="248" w="390"><p font-size="16pt" align="center">Centered in this sky view—not at the center of the universe.</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="13pt">The oval maps arrival directions, not a physical shell. Mottling is schematic, not measured CMB temperature data.</p></grid-item></grid></section>